// Welcome to live coding
// Live coding: you write code that
// makes music, and change it while
// it plays. The code is the
// instrument.
//
// Lines that start with // are
// comments: notes for you, they make
// no sound.
//
// Try: tap ▶ Play at the top, then
// ■ Stop. Then tap Next, at the
// bottom, for step 2.

$: s("bd sd")
// ---
// Change it while it plays
// Try: tap ▶ Play. While it plays,
// change sd into hh. The Play button
// is now ⟳ Update: tap it.
// The music changes on the beat,
// without stopping.
//
// More sounds to try: cp, rim, lt.

$: s("bd sd")
// ---
// The status line
// While music plays, the line under
// the title shows the tempo and the
// cycle: 30 cpm · cycle 12.
//
// A cycle is the loop a pattern
// repeats. Here bd and sd share one
// cycle: each gets half of it.
//
// Try: write "bd sd hh" and Update.
// Three sounds share the cycle, so
// each one is shorter.

$: s("bd sd")
// ---
// Mistakes are fine
// Try: play, then delete the last "
// of the line below and Update.
// The status line turns red and says
// where the problem is. Tap it to
// select the faulty code.
// The music keeps playing what worked
// last: a mistake never stops a set.
// Put the " back and Update.

$: s("bd sd hh sd")
// ---
// Layers
// Each line that starts with $: is a
// layer. Layers play together.
// ~ is a rest: nothing plays there.
//
// Try: add a layer of your own:
// $: s("hh hh hh hh")
// and Update.
//
// Lesson 1 is done. In the Library,
// lesson 2 shows how to edit code
// quickly with your fingers.

$: s("bd sd")
$: s("~ cp")
